DPPO (vendored excerpts)
=======================

Repository: https://github.com/irom-princeton/dppo
Commit: cc7234ad7ff39a8f32de3af903606723a16f0648
License: MIT

Files copied into this directory, and the paths they came from:

- modules.py
  model/diffusion/modules.py
  model/common/modules.py
- vit.py
  model/common/vit.py
- unet1d.py
  model/diffusion/unet.py
- diffusion.py
  model/diffusion/diffusion.py
  model/diffusion/sampling.py

The ViT encoder is attributed by DPPO to IBRL
(https://github.com/hengyuan-hu/ibrl). The cosine schedule and the 1D
residual blocks are attributed by DPPO to Diffuser
(https://github.com/jannerm/diffuser) and to Diffusion Policy
(https://github.com/real-stanford/diffusion_policy). Those notes are kept in
the file headers. The text below is the license of the DPPO revision that
was copied. The excerpts are not imported from a DPPO install.

What changed relative to that revision:

- einops rearranges are torch reshape / transpose / flatten.
- hydra instantiation, wandb, and the RL fine-tuning classes are not copied.
- ResidualMLP / cond_mlp is not copied; the Can image config does not use it.
- PatchEmbed1 is not copied; the Can image config uses embed2.
- Random shift runs only in train mode.
- DDIM eta is fixed at 0. Sampling takes the initial noise as an argument
  and does not draw a later noise tensor when that coefficient is zero.
- Attention uses the math SDPA kernel.
- Image history uses the sliced time length when splitting cameras.

